</span></div>
    </div>
          <div class="views-row">
      <div class="views-field views-field-rendered-entity"><span class="field-content">    
<div class="node--embedded">
    <h2>
        <a href="/code/17/111" rel="bookmark"><span class="field field--name-title field--type-string field--label-hidden">Chapter 17.111 Portable Signs</span>
</a>
    </h2>
    



<div class="clearfix text-formatted field field--label-hidden field--name-field-prefix-note field--type-text-long ck-content"><div class="field__item"><p>(Added by Ordinance 192204, effective July 25, 2026.)</p></div></div><div class="views-element-container">
<div class="mb-6 view view-eva view-city-code-list view-id-city_code_list view-display-id-eva_embedded_code_chapters js-view-dom-id-de3bc87849f36a3f29f790dca270af6fbb8854779777f44ec84c19834fd15301">
  
    

  
  

  
  
  

  
  

  
  </div>
</div>
<div class="views-element-container">
<div class="mb-6 view view-eva view-city-code-list view-id-city_code_list view-display-id-eva_embedded_code_sections js-view-dom-id-bf6d7a982d2a793819130fd7ed9fafd5146ecfd4bae1ea36e892cf846f1fb3a4">
  
    

  
  

          <div class="views-row">
           
<div class="node--embedded">
    <h3>
        <a href="/code/17/111/010" rel="bookmark"><span class="field field--name-title field--type-string field--label-hidden">17.111.010 Definitions.</span>
</a>
    </h3>
    



<div class="clearfix text-formatted field field--label-hidden field--name-field-section-body field--type-text-long ck-content"><div class="field__item"><ol class="code-list"><li><strong>A. Curb ramp.</strong><span> A sloped connection that is cut through or built up to a curb. Curb ramps may be perpendicular or parallel to the curb or to the street they serve or be a combination thereof</span>.</li><li><strong>B. Building.</strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;As defined in Portland City Code Title 33, Planning and Zoning.</li><li><strong>C. Crosswalk.&nbsp;</strong>&nbsp;<span>A <strong>marked crosswalk</strong> is any portion of a roadway at an intersection or elsewhere that is distinctly indicated for pedestrian crossing by lines or other markings on the surface of the roadway. An <strong>unmarked crosswalk</strong> is the imagined extension of a sidewalk or shoulder across a street at an intersection. An unmarked crosswalk exists at all intersections unless specifically marked otherwise.</span></li><li><span><strong>D. Frontage zone. </strong>A<strong>&nbsp;</strong>linear portion of the sidewalk corridor, adjacent to the edge of the right-of-way (or property line).</span></li><li><span><strong>E. Furnishing zone. </strong>A linear portion of the sidewalk corridor, adjacent to the curb that contains elements such as street trees, signal poles, utility poles, streetlights, controller boxes, hydrants, traffic signs, street signs, parking signs, parking meters, driveway aprons, planting strip, or street furniture.&nbsp;</span></li><li><strong>F. Pedestrian through zone.&nbsp;</strong>&nbsp;The area of the sidewalk corridor intended for pedestrian travel. The pedestrian through zone should be entirely free of above-ground permanent and temporary objects in order to provide an obstruction-free, continuous corridor for people to travel.</li><li><strong>G. Portable sign.&nbsp; </strong>A movable sign that is not attached to a structure or the ground.&nbsp; Portable signs include A-boards, portable reader boards, and similar signs.<strong>&nbsp;</strong></li><li><strong>H. Right-of-way</strong>. <span>The area between property lines of a street, easement, tract or other area dedicated to the movement of vehicles, pedestrians and/or goods, as defined in Portland City Code Section 16.90.302.</span></li><li><strong>I. Sidewalk.</strong> The portion of the street between the curb lines or lateral lines of roadway and the adjacent property lines intended for use by pedestrians as defined in Portland City Code Section 16.90.330 <span>and includes all areas of a pedestrian plaza as defined under Chapter 17.43.</span></li><li><strong>J. Street.&nbsp;</strong>&nbsp;The area dedicated to public use for public street purposes and includes, but is not limited to, roadways, parkways, and alleys.&nbsp;</li><li><span><strong>K. Transit platform.</strong>&nbsp;Any Portland Streetcar platform or TriMet bus stop, bus layover zone, or light rail station platform. This definition applies, but is not limited, to transit facilities located on public or private streets, in transit centers, and on the Transit Mall.</span></li></ol></div></div><div class="views-element-container">
<div class="mb-6 view view-eva view-city-code-list view-id-city_code_list view-display-id-eva_embedded_code_chapters js-view-dom-id-b1ae807757990e9e905e595267a16350d47c6a846bdf3bdc653f43fa3d43dc3b">
  
    

  
  

  
  
  

  
  

  
  </div>
</div>
<div class="views-element-container">
<div class="mb-6 view view-eva view-city-code-list view-id-city_code_list view-display-id-eva_embedded_code_sections js-view-dom-id-cd5327f409673baf1d61d91d0061e0c4d10bd6e91e892ace79511bb43157c224">
  
    

  
  

  
  
  

  
  

  
  </div>
</div>

</div>

    </div>
          <div class="views-row">
           
<div class="node--embedded">
    <h3>
        <a href="/code/17/111/020" rel="bookmark"><span class="field field--name-title field--type-string field--label-hidden">17.111.020 Portable Signs.</span>
</a>
    </h3>
    



<div class="clearfix text-formatted field field--label-hidden field--name-field-section-body field--type-text-long ck-content"><div class="field__item"><p>Portable signs may be placed within the right-of-way as allowed by this Chapter and in accordance with the requirements of Portland City Code Title 32. Other signs, sign structures, and awnings that extend from private property over rights of way are regulated by Title 32.</p></div></div><div class="views-element-container">
<div class="mb-6 view view-eva view-city-code-list view-id-city_code_list view-display-id-eva_embedded_code_chapters js-view-dom-id-d116486830253db88b64e5d4b97cf702d91da962567a22939162e4b6723de504">
  
    

  
  

  
  
  

  
  

  
  </div>
</div>
<div class="views-element-container">
<div class="mb-6 view view-eva view-city-code-list view-id-city_code_list view-display-id-eva_embedded_code_sections js-view-dom-id-12359fb7de4b12b856b26ce6fd255994a3c848e61f75662839547ce9b7922a5b">
  
    

  
  

  
  
  

  
  

  
  </div>
</div>

</div>

    </div>
          <div class="views-row">
           
<div class="node--embedded">
    <h3>
        <a href="/code/17/111/030" rel="bookmark"><span class="field field--name-title field--type-string field--label-hidden">17.111.030 Portable Signs Standards.</span>
</a>
    </h3>
    



<div class="clearfix text-formatted field field--label-hidden field--name-field-section-body field--type-text-long ck-content"><div class="field__item"><ol class="code-list"><li><strong>A.</strong><span><strong>&nbsp;&nbsp; </strong></span>General.&nbsp; Portable signs that meet the requirements described in Title 32 of the Portland City Code, and meet the requirements of this subsection, are allowed.&nbsp;</li><li><strong>B.</strong><span><strong>&nbsp;&nbsp; </strong></span>Additional maintenance standards. Portable sign owners are responsible for keeping portable signs well maintained, standing upright, and properly placed outside of the pedestrian through zone.</li><li><strong>C.</strong><span><strong>&nbsp;&nbsp; </strong></span>Prohibited right-of-way placement. Portable signs cannot be located:<ol><li><strong>1.</strong><span><strong>&nbsp;&nbsp; </strong></span>Within the roadway:</li><li><strong>2.</strong><span><strong>&nbsp;&nbsp; </strong></span>Within a traffic island, median or traffic circle;</li><li><strong>3.</strong><span><strong>&nbsp;&nbsp; </strong></span>Within five feet of any crosswalk;</li><li><strong>4.</strong><span><strong>&nbsp;&nbsp; </strong></span>Within five feet of a fire hydrant;</li><li><strong>5.</strong><span><strong>&nbsp;&nbsp; </strong></span>Within five feet of a drinking fountain;</li><li><strong>6.</strong><span><strong>&nbsp;&nbsp; </strong></span>Within five feet of any public art or public monument, as defined in Portland City Code Chapter 5.40, excluding original art murals, as defined in City Code Chapter 4;</li><li><strong>7.</strong><span><strong>&nbsp;&nbsp; </strong></span>Within five feet of any driveway, alley, or curb ramp;</li><li><strong>8.</strong><span><strong>&nbsp;&nbsp; </strong></span>Within five feet of an entry to a building entrance ramp;</li><li><strong>9.</strong><span><strong>&nbsp;&nbsp; </strong></span>Within five feet of a marked accessible parking space;</li><li><strong>10.</strong> Within a transit platform unless allowed by Portland Streetcar or TriMet;</li><li><strong>11.</strong> Within the corner of two intersecting sidewalk corridors, as determined by the adjacent property lines extended;</li><li><strong>12.</strong> Further than six inches from the curb if placed in the furnishing zone:</li><li><strong>13.</strong> Further than six inches from the adjoining business if placed in the frontage zone;</li><li><strong>14.</strong> Where the sign creates less than 36 inches of clearance within the right-of-way;</li><li><strong>15.</strong> Where the sign may cause damage to any landscaping, including but not limited to lawn, flowers, shrubs or trees;</li><li><strong>16.</strong> Where the sign obstructs access to parked vehicles;</li><li><strong>17.</strong> Where the sign obscures any fixed regulatory or informational sign;</li><li><strong>18.</strong> In an area outside of the adjoining public right-of-way of the business associated with the portable sign; or</li><li><strong>19.</strong> In any place, manner or situation that may be prohibited by any other section of Portland City Code.</li></ol></li></ol></div></div><div class="views-element-container">
<div class="mb-6 view view-eva view-city-code-list view-id-city_code_list view-display-id-eva_embedded_code_chapters js-view-dom-id-12c234a47c608c26a6e191a4d9352519bef8b03039587bfa47ee3972766c0bc7">
  
    

  
  

  
  
  

  
  

  
  </div>
</div>
<div class="views-element-container">
<div class="mb-6 view view-eva view-city-code-list view-id-city_code_list view-display-id-eva_embedded_code_sections js-view-dom-id-f98113225cf669f8ff3c7d508d654e04dd290ce90b24cd7a0822a14113d9c6a2">
  
    

  
  

  
  
  

  
  

  
  </div>
</div>

</div>

    </div>
          <div class="views-row">
           
<div class="node--embedded">
    <h3>
        <a href="/code/17/111/040" rel="bookmark"><span class="field field--name-title field--type-string field--label-hidden">17.111.040 Violations.</span>
</a>
    </h3>
    



<div class="clearfix text-formatted field field--label-hidden field--name-field-section-body field--type-text-long ck-content"><div class="field__item"><ol class="code-list"><li><strong>A.</strong><span><strong>&nbsp;&nbsp; </strong></span>The following constitute violations of this Chapter:<ol><li><strong>1.</strong><span><strong>&nbsp;&nbsp; </strong></span>Any failure, refusal or neglect to comply with any provision of this Chapter;</li><li><strong>2.</strong><span><strong>&nbsp;&nbsp; </strong></span>Allowing or causing a condition that threatens to injure the public health or safety, or threatens to damage public or private property; or</li><li><strong>3.</strong><span><strong>&nbsp;&nbsp; </strong></span>Any failure, refusal or neglect to correct or remove any sign, awning, strobe light, banner or balloon that does not comply with the provisions of this Chapter, after being required to do so by the City Administrator or their designee.</li></ol></li><li><strong>B.</strong><span><strong>&nbsp;&nbsp; </strong></span>Each specific incident and each day of non-compliance will be considered a separate violation of this Chapter.</li><li><strong>C.</strong><span><strong>&nbsp;&nbsp; </strong>The City Administrator or their designee may inspect and enforce compliance related to rules and regulations in this Chapter. Enforcement of rules and regulations in this Chapter will be in accordance with TRN-8.14 (Right-Of-Way Use Enforcement Program).</span> Violations will be subject to fine per the Transportation Fee Schedule (per TRN-3.450).</li><li><strong>D.</strong><span><strong>&nbsp;&nbsp; </strong></span>In addition to fees described in this section, where a portable sign has been the subject of multiple citations, the sign may be removed and the owner charged, in addition to any other fee, the administrative costs of removal of a portable sign.</li></ol></div></div><div class="views-element-container">
<div class="mb-6 view view-eva view-city-code-list view-id-city_code_list view-display-id-eva_embedded_code_chapters js-view-dom-id-9e43732afefaaae67d604e9cd497977c1535ee41811d00365853f9ab36f69774">
  
    

  
  

  
  
  

  
  

  
  </div>
</div>
<div class="views-element-container">
<div class="mb-6 view view-eva view-city-code-list view-id-city_code_list view-display-id-eva_embedded_code_sections js-view-dom-id-54dd731a6108fc5ff0a110ca08dfd173f80b751c1119b04000a6a4eea4256e79">
  
    

  
  

  
  
  

  
  

  
  </div>
</div>

</div>

    </div>
  
  
  

  
  

  
  </div>
</div>

</div>
</span></div>
